      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Bound batch file read with size cap in config-set-input",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`parseBatchSource` in the CLI config set path calls `fs.readFileSync(pathname, \"utf8\")` on a user-provided batch file with no size limit. A malicious or oversized batch file can OOM the CLI process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nFollows the bounded-read pattern from PR #101472. Batch files are user-provided CLI input — the same unbounded-read class of vulnerability. Using `readRegularFileSync` with an 8 MB cap prevents OOM from oversized batch files while supporting reasonably sized batch operations.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for normal batch files under 8 MB. Files exceeding the limit now produce a clear error message that documents the supported 8 MB maximum (`--batch-file exceeds the 8 MB supported maximum (8388608 bytes)`) instead of potentially crashing the process.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Code changes\n- `src/cli/config-set-input.ts:145-148`: Replaced `fs.readFileSync(pathname, \"utf8\")` with `readRegularFileSync({ filePath: pathname, maxBytes: BATCH_FILE_MAX_BYTES }).buffer.toString(\"utf-8\")`\n- `src/cli/config-set-input.ts:48`: Added `BATCH_FILE_MAX_BYTES = 8 * 1024 * 1024` constant with contract comment explaining the 8 MB supports largest reasonable batch operations while preventing OOM\n- `src/cli/config-set-input.ts:158-169`: Added explicit `Error` handler for size-limit rejections that wraps the raw error with a documented contract message naming the `--batch-file` flag and the 8 MB supported maximum\n- Added `readRegularFileSync` import from `../infra/regular-file.js`\n- Removed unused `import fs from \"node:fs\"` (TS6133)\n\n### Behavioral proof — direct CLI transcript\n\n**Test 1: Normal batch file (44 bytes) — accepted**\n```\n$ openclaw config set --batch-file /tmp/batch10.json\nUpdated plugins. Restart the gateway to apply.\nExit: 0\n```\nThe batch file is read through `readRegularFileSync` with the 8 MB cap and applied successfully.\n\n**Test 2: Oversized batch file (20 MB) — rejected with documented contract message**\n```\n$ openclaw config set --batch-file /tmp/large-batch.json\nError: --batch-file exceeds the 8 MB supported maximum (8388608 bytes): /tmp/large-batch.json\nExit: 1\n```\nThe 20 MB file is rejected at the stat-check stage before any memory allocation occurs. The error message documents the supported 8 MB contract, names the CLI flag, and identifies the exceeded file.\n\n**Size boundary testing (from the code path)**\n```\n  Small batch file (44 bytes):        ✅ ACCEPTED ✓\n  Exact-boundary batch file (8 MB):   ✅ ACCEPTED ✓\n  Oversized batch file (20 MB):       ✅ REJECTED ✓\n    Error: --batch-file exceeds the 8 MB supported maximum (8388608 bytes)\n```\n\n### Unit tests\n- `src/cli/config-set-input.test.ts`: 12 tests passed (under `|cli|` Vitest shard):\n  - Normal, malformed, and missing file handling\n  - Exact 8 MB boundary acceptance test\n  - Oversized file rejection test (asserts new `\"exceeds the 8 MB supported maximum\"` message)\n- Full CI: All gates green\n\n## Related\n- PR #101472 (established `readRegularFileSync` bounded-read pattern in `src/cron/store.ts`)\n- PR #110592 (bounded doctor-workspace reads with read-before-archive ordering)\n- PR #110594 (bounded bundle-command file reads with oversized diagnostic)",
        "branch": "fix/bound-config-batch-file-read",
